-- title:
--   Square-zero descent of two rigidifications to a common correspondence
-- statement:
--   **Numerical and arithmetic data.** Fix primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero field realised as the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr\,x\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Let $vdet:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ be a homomorphism characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **The indefinite side and its moduli.** Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and is a division algebra at exactly the finite places above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), and let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order in it. Let $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, with its point assignment `pt`, be a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`). Let $n\geq 3$ be coprime to $N$ and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$, let $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with `ptF` be a fine moduli space for such curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), and let $G$ act on $M$ through $\rho$ with labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ as a level-twist action (`hρ`). Let $p:M\to\mathcal X$ be a morphism over the base (`hp`), invariant under the $G$-action (`hρp`), and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ let $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with `ptT` be a coarse moduli space for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), and let $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ be morphisms over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) which on points forget the extra level (`hd₀`) and pass to a level-$\ell$ isogeny quotient (`hd₁`). Let $a_r,a_{\bar r}:\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ be morphisms over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite side and the group $\Gamma^{t}$.** Let $a_1,b_1\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); let $\Lambda_1$ be a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$, $n_1$ a finite idèle in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $\operatorname{meetOrder} R_1\,n_1$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), $\iota_0$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and $v$ a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. Let $\Gamma^{t}$ be the subgroup of units characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units of $R_1$ away from $v$, let $s_\ell$ and $sf_\ell$ ($\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$) satisfy the four clauses of `hs` (the idèle $sf_\ell$ equals $s_\ell$ at every place not above $r$, equals $1$ at the places above $r$, the product of the diagonal idèle of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\operatorname{meetOrder}R_1\,n_1$ relative to $\Lambda_1$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in its prime Hecke set at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\operatorname{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), and let $\Gamma^t_\ell=\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). Let $\bar w$ be a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The base curve over the residue field.** Assume $\Lambda$ contains every rational integer (`hΛℤ`) and let $coord:\Lambda\to Zp2\,r\times Zp2\,r$ be an order coordinate system (`hcoord`). Over $k_0:=Onr/(\pi)$ let $A_0$ be a fake elliptic curve with level-$N$ structure, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ formal coordinates of length $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$ with $A_0$ a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`), and $e,e':\Gamma^t\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) require respectively: each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure; $e(\gamma\gamma')$ agrees with $e\gamma'$ followed by $e\gamma$ after multiplication by suitable powers of $r$; integral scalars $\gamma$ give multiplication maps up to $r$-powers, and conversely $e\gamma$ being a multiplication up to $r$-powers forces $\gamma$ to be a rational scalar; for every injective embedding of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and of $X_0.\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on nilpotent formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; the action of $\Gamma^t$ on a full level-$n$ structure is given by labels in $\Lambda$, multiplicative modulo $n$ and matching scalars modulo $n$; and every degree-$r^{d}$ level-preserving self-isogeny of a geometric fibre of $A_0$ over an algebraically closed field comes from some $e\gamma$ up to $r$-powers. Further, $R_2\le R_1$ is an order (`hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators relative to $R_1$ (`hR₂r`), and $\hat e:R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ is a family over the base (`hê`) subject to `hE5a` (additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, level preservation), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, multiplicativity, integral scalars), `hE5c` (composition with the conjugate gives multiplication by the reduced norm), `hE5d` (compatibility with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma^t$) and `hE5e` (a common conjugating matrix $g$ realising both the $\Gamma^t$-family and the $R_2$-family on formal coordinates, as in `hE2`).
--
--   **The formal-module dictionary.** Let $\iota:Zp2\,r\to Onr$ be a ring map, $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`), $MD$ a moduli package over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ a rule attaching to each rigidified object over an $r$-nilpotent ring a point of $MD$, subject to the three clauses of `hη`: over Noetherian rings $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidified objects exactly when they are isomorphic, $\eta$ is natural in the ring, and every point of $MD$ is, locally on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, in the image of $\eta$ on admissible objects. Let $E_0$ be a ring map from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\Phi.\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ which is injective and has an integral image up to one common power $r^{m}$ in both directions (`hE₀`). Let $eD$ compare the functor $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,MD$ with the product of $\operatorname{corep} Onr$ and the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$ on Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras; it is assumed natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), compatible with the structure maps to $Onr$ (`hfstD`), to turn the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points into the twisted action on Deligne data (`hGLD`), to turn a $\varpi$-translate into the Frobenius twist by $1$ with unchanged datum (`hPiD`), and $\varpi$-translates are assumed to exist (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Transport data.** Let $\kappa:Onr/(\pi)\to Onr/(r)$ be compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), $n_0\in\mathbb N$ and $\beta_0$ an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). Let $P_0$ be a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$. Let $A_{0w}$ over $k_0$, with morphisms $aw,aw'$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ from $A_0$ (`hALw`), and $bw,bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ (`hBSw`) preserving level (`hBSwlev`), be such that `hJOINTw` holds: for every injective embedding of the centraliser into $M_2(K_0)$ there is one $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ which simultaneously conjugates the $\Gamma^t$-family as in `hE2` and realises $aw$ followed by $bw$ by an element whose image is $r^{k_w'}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The point map $\Xi$ and the evenness package.** Let $\Xi$ assign to each rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with structure map $\psi:Onr\to B$ a point of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.GPoint}\,\mathcal O\,MD$ over $B$, subject to: `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the $Onr$-leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $Fr^{k}\circ\psi$ of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality along pullbacks of curves and of rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance under an isomorphism of curves together with a comparison of the two rigidifications up to $r$-powers), and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, the explicit value of $\Xi$ as $\eta$ applied to a rigidified object $t$ obtained by rig transport with exponent $j\le 1$, admissible for the twist $Fr^{-j}\circ\psi$). Let $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, and assume: `heqΓ` (over connected $B$, if two rigidifications of the same curve are translates of one another by $e\gamma$, their $\Xi$-images are related by the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$), `heqW` (the analogous statement for an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ when $\bar r$ is invertible in $B$, with $\iota_0(\bar w)$ in place of $\iota_0(\gamma)$), `hK1`–`hK4` (existence, uniqueness up to isomorphism-with-comparison, pullback along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, and lifting along square-zero surjections, of pairs $(E,\varrho)$ whose $\Xi$-leg is the twist of $\psi$ by $-vdet(g_0)$ and whose $eD$-image is $g_0^{-1}$-twisted-related to a prescribed Deligne datum), and `hC0e`, `hC0u` (existence over connected $B$, and uniqueness of the underlying section, of a full level-$n$ structure on $E$ which is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification). Finally $\Theta_f$ compares the product of $\operatorname{corep}Onr$, $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$ and the constant functor $G$ with the nilpotent points of $fM$, and is assumed natural (`hΘnat`) and to take the expected values, namely the level-$n$ point twisted by $\rho(g^{-1})$ (`hΘval`) and, after composing with $p$, the coarse point of $E$ (`hΘvalc`).
--
--   **The data of the statement.** Let $pB:B\to B_0$ be a surjective morphism of Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, such that any two elements of $\ker pB$ have product zero (`hsqB`), and such that every idempotent of $B_0$ is $0$ or $1$ (`hconn₀`). Let $\psi:Onr\to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and $P,P'$ two Deligne data over $B$ with the same base change to $B_0$ (`hred`). Let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, and let $\varrho_1,\varrho_2$ be two rigidifications of $E$ relative to $A_0$ and the twisted map $Fr^{-vdet(g_0)}\circ\psi$, that is, each consists of a reduction $E_b$ of $E$ over $B/(\pi)$ with comparison $g_b$, a base change $A_b$ of $A_0$ along the residue leg with comparison $g_A$, an exponent $d$, and a level-preserving isogeny pair $(\varphi,\varphi')$ of degree $r^{d}$ between $E_b$ and $A_b$. Assume $\Xi$ assigns to $(E,\varrho_1)$ the leg $Fr^{-vdet(g_0)}\circ\psi$ (`h₁ψ`) and an $eD$-image which is $g_0^{-1}$-twisted-related to $(\psi,P)$ (`h₁P`), and likewise for $(E,\varrho_2)$ with $P'$ in place of $P$ (`h₂ψ`, `h₂P`). Assume finally that one and the same full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ is the height-normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho_1$ (`hPn₁`) and along $\varrho_2$ (`hPn₂`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Then there exist a fake elliptic curve $E_0$ over $B_0$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, a morphism $g:E_0.A\to E.A$ exhibiting $E_0$ as the pullback of $E$ along $pB$ (compatibly with the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level structure), and two rigidifications $\varrho_{1,0},\varrho_{2,0}$ of $E_0$ relative to the twisted map $Fr^{-vdet(g_0)}\circ(pB\circ\psi)$, such that $\varrho_{1,0}$ is the pullback of $\varrho_1$ and $\varrho_{2,0}$ is the pullback of $\varrho_2$ along $pB$ and $g$, together with:
--
--   - a morphism $ib:\varrho_{1,0}.E_b.A\to\varrho_{2,0}.E_b.A$ with $ib$ followed by $\varrho_{2,0}.g_b$ equal to $\varrho_{1,0}.g_b$, and $ib$ followed by $\varrho_{2,0}.E_b.f$ equal to $\varrho_{1,0}.E_b.f$;
--
--   - a morphism $uA:\varrho_{2,0}.A_b.A\to\varrho_{1,0}.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho_{2,0}.A_b$ as a pullback of $\varrho_{1,0}.A_b$ along the identity of $B_0/(\pi)$, with $uA$ followed by $\varrho_{1,0}.g_A$ equal to $\varrho_{2,0}.g_A$;
--
--   - natural numbers $i,j$ such that $ib$ followed by $\varrho_{2,0}.\varphi$, then by $uA$, then by multiplication by $r^{i}$ on $\varrho_{1,0}.A_b$, equals $\varrho_{1,0}.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j}$ on $\varrho_{1,0}.A_b$.
--
--   This is the descent step of the rigidity argument for the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary: two rigidifications of one fake elliptic curve over a $\pi$-nilpotent base which carry the same normalised level-$n$ transport are shown to acquire, after restriction along a square-zero surjection onto a connected quotient, a comparison of the prescribed shape (an identification of the reductions together with compatible presentations, up to powers of $r$). It supplies the input of the rigidity lemma along square-zero thickenings used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_lift_unique_locally_of_value_of_squareZero), which deduces local uniqueness of the lift of a family of points to the fine moduli scheme.
